### Topic 42 - Transactions (VS Code "REST Client" extension)
@base = http://localhost:8080/api

########## The real bank API ##########

### Accounts (look at "version" - it increases with every update)
GET {{base}}/accounts

### Total money in the bank - transfers must never change it
GET {{base}}/accounts/total

### Correct transfer
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccount": "ACC-1001", "toAccount": "ACC-1002", "amount": 250.00 }

### Not enough money -> 422, nothing changes (rollback)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccount": "ACC-1001", "toAccount": "ACC-1002", "amount": 99999 }

### Unknown account -> 404
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccount": "ACC-9999", "toAccount": "ACC-1002", "amount": 10 }

### Successful transfers
GET {{base}}/transfers

### Audit log (REQUIRES_NEW rows survive rollbacks)
GET {{base}}/audit

########## Demo scenarios: each resets to Alice 1000 / Bob 500 and moves 100 ##########

### Reset
POST {{base}}/demo/reset

### 1. Failure midway INSIDE @Transactional -> moneyLost: false
POST {{base}}/demo/rollback

### 2. Same failure WITHOUT a transaction -> moneyLost: true
POST {{base}}/demo/no-transaction

### 3. Checked exception, default rules -> committed, moneyLost: true
POST {{base}}/demo/checked-exception

### 4. Checked exception with rollbackFor -> moneyLost: false
POST {{base}}/demo/checked-exception-rollback-for

### 5. Self-invocation -> @Transactional ignored, moneyLost: true
POST {{base}}/demo/self-invocation

### 6. Insufficient funds in the real transfer -> rollback, attempt audited
POST {{base}}/demo/insufficient-funds

### 7. Optimistic locking with @Version -> second update rejected
POST {{base}}/demo/optimistic-lock
